# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# SOS redouble (`other_conventions.sos_redouble.play`; convention-card
# competitive_bidding/sos_redouble; "25 More Bridge Conventions You
# Should Know", chapter 22): when a low-level contract of ours is
# doubled for penalty, a redouble asks partner to choose another suit
# rather than showing strength.
#
# Written for the one place where the engine knows the double has
# become a penalty double: our one-level opening doubled for takeout and
# passed round by the doubler's partner, 1x (X) P (P). Opener redoubles
# with three cards or fewer in his suit (a short minor opening); with
# four or more he passes and plays it. Responder then bids his longest
# other suit, the cheapest of equals. Notes: sos-redouble.notes.md.

module sos-redouble "SOS redouble"
  needs  base
  skill  competitive_bidding/sos_redouble
  card   other_conventions.sos_redouble.play

after 1x (X) P (P)
  XX  "SOS: {x} is short, pick another suit"
      alert  artificial
      shows x<=3
      sets  ask=sos
      priority 1
  P   "To play: four or more {x}"
      shows x>=4
      priority 1

# Responder: his longest suit other than opener's, cheapest of equals.
after 1x (X) P (P) XX (P)
  cheapest(C) "Rescue: clubs"     shows C>=D | x is D, C>=H | x is H, C>=S | x is S
      when  x is not C
      priority 1
  cheapest(D) "Rescue: diamonds"  shows D>C | x is C, D>=H | x is H, D>=S | x is S
      when  x is not D
      priority 1
  cheapest(H) "Rescue: hearts"    shows H>C | x is C, H>D | x is D, H>=S | x is S
      when  x is not H
      priority 1
  cheapest(S) "Rescue: spades"    shows S>C | x is C, S>D | x is D, S>H | x is H
      when  x is not S
      priority 1
